{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member","id":864291,"title":"Endless Vitae from a willing Uratha Pack member?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-12T08:00:02-07:00","id":864291,"title":"Endless Vitae from a willing Uratha Pack member?","content":"A friend and I are running a round robin style game set in modern day using the 2nd edition Vampire and Werewolf rules. The situation is one of survival. As I feed, it causes 1 lethal per point of Vitae taken. If the friendly werewolf can regenerate lethal so quickly.. do I not basically have an endless supply of Vitae if we have downtime for the procedure and for his healing?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this has been covered, I searched but didn't find any mention of this specific question. We are in a setting on the verge of zombie apocalypse. My vampire is an older Ordo Gangrel who was Embraced on the night of his First Change, the werewolf is a decendant, his grandson. We are in a small rural area, a town with less than 800 people. As far as we know I am the only vampire for miles, recently awoken from Torpor so I don't have a good source to feed on just yet. My Blood Potency is at 3 so I can't subsist off of animals.<br /> <br /> Is there also information about how long you can store vitae and if it's potency dilutes? Like in 1st edition, it was harder to store and drink cold blood, like from a blood bank.<br /> <br /> I could not find rules in the 2nd ed Vampire book detailing the effects of werewolf blood as was detailed in 1st edition. As far as I am aware, I could feed fully from this werewolf and he can heal it all away after a short period of rest, rinse and repeat.. I am a member of his pack and his totem, albiet a minor one, has accepted me due to my heritage.<br /> <br /> Questions in summary:<br /> <br /> 1) Are there rules for storing Vitae? How long, how much is needed, etc. I want to store vitae in a fridge or perhaps blood bags.<br /> <br /> 2) Can you feed endlessly from a friendly werewolf? Does the book talk about types of blood and its effects on Kindred, such as in 1st edition?<br /> <br /> <br /> Any help on this would be great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:19:57-07:00","id":864303,"title":"","content":"Vitae turns back into regular blood pretty quickly outside a vampire (/revenant/ghoul/whatever). You can feed off cold blood though. You just need to drink [Blood Potency x 2] pints per vitae gained. <br /> <br /> Werewolf blood doesn't have any particular effects in second edition. Without the Taste of the Strange merit it just counts as regular human blood. (And with it it can substitute for vitae for elders, which at bp3 isn't an issue). You'd probably want to avoid giving them the drained condition but as long as you were careful you could get 4 vitae an hour form them without them needing to spend essence, which while not exactly &quot;endless&quot; is pretty close for most purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:21:47-07:00","id":864304,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that Vitae doesn't store well at all. I think the rule in my game is that, short of magical means, vitae loses potency in (BP) minutes, becoming a decayed mix of blood types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:27:32-07:00","id":864308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member#post864291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend and I are running a round robin style game set in modern day using the 2nd edition Vampire and Werewolf rules. The situation is one of survival. As I feed, it causes 1 lethal per point of Vitae taken. If the friendly werewolf can regenerate lethal so quickly.. do I not basically have an endless supply of Vitae if we have downtime for the procedure and for his healing?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this has been covered, I searched but didn't find any mention of this specific question. We are in a setting on the verge of zombie apocalypse. My vampire is an older Ordo Gangrel who was Embraced on the night of his First Change, the werewolf is a decendant, his grandson. We are in a small rural area, a town with less than 800 people. As far as we know I am the only vampire for miles, recently awoken from Torpor so I don't have a good source to feed on just yet. My Blood Potency is at 3 so I can't subsist off of animals.<br /> <br /> Is there also information about how long you can store vitae and if it's potency dilutes? Like in 1st edition, it was harder to store and drink cold blood, like from a blood bank.<br /> <br /> I could not find rules in the 2nd ed Vampire book detailing the effects of werewolf blood as was detailed in 1st edition. As far as I am aware, I could feed fully from this werewolf and he can heal it all away after a short period of rest, rinse and repeat.. I am a member of his pack and his totem, albiet a minor one, has accepted me due to my heritage.<br /> <br /> Questions in summary:<br /> <br /> 1) Are there rules for storing Vitae? How long, how much is needed, etc. I want to store vitae in a fridge or perhaps blood bags.<br /> <br /> 2) Can you feed endlessly from a friendly werewolf? Does the book talk about types of blood and its effects on Kindred, such as in 1st edition?<br /> <br /> <br /> Any help on this would be great!</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Not really, barring blood magic. Vitae remains vitae on a rule of narrative basis, for lack of a better term. I think scene is the limit, but I that I can't recall for sure. I know you can spike someone's drink with it, but you can't keep it in your fridge.<br /> <br /> 2) As long as a werewolf can regenerate, a vampire can feed from it (this is a feature, not a bug). Also assuming you purchase Unnatural Affinity once the vampire's Blood Potency gets too high to feed off humans. So far, in second edition, supernatural being blood is the same as human blood as far as feeding goes. It keeps things simple (though I think demon blood does odd things if you check out the Demon ST Guide).<br /> <br /> That being said, feeding off a werewolf isn't always the best idea in the world, for a lot of reasons. But that's another issue entirely...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-12-2016, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:30:07-07:00","id":864312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member?p=864303#post864303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae turns back into regular blood pretty quickly outside a vampire (/revenant/ghoul/whatever). You can feed off cold blood though. You just need to drink [Blood Potency x 2] pints per vitae gained.<br /> <br /> Werewolf blood doesn't have any particular effects in second edition. Without the Taste of the Strange merit it just counts as regular human blood. (And with it it can substitute for vitae for elders, which at bp3 isn't an issue). You'd probably want to avoid giving them the drained condition but as long as you were careful you could get 4 vitae an hour form them without them needing to spend essence, which while not exactly &quot;endless&quot; is pretty close for most purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We sort of house ruled it this way, as it being basically normal human blood. Which is a great thing to know it is legit. I was hoping there would be something that would let me store vitae outside of the Reilquary ritual.Is there a page reference for the BP x 2 points per vitae mention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:32:52-07:00","id":864315,"title":"","content":"At best, you might say that ex-vitae has just enough magic left in it that an elder vamp could gain sustenance from it using the cold blood rules without spending willpower. I mean, they would need to drink at least a gallon and a half of the stuff. Even trace vitaeness would add up eventually.<br /> <br /> Edit: The cold blood stuff is on page 95. And it's pints, not points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-12-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:06:36-07:00","id":864330,"title":"","content":"I thought one pint was the same as one point of Vitae? Did they change this in 2nd edition? The average human body holds 6-10 pints of blood. When I ran it back in 1st edition, I just said each average human held 7 pints or 1 pint per health level. If it is stored, Id need 6 pints of blood to get 1 point of vitae.. Per the 2nd edition rules, I can't really store viable Vitae for more than a night, even if I do it falls under the BP x 2 rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:20:32-07:00","id":864335,"title":"","content":"I have run into the same thing in game. However. We have house ruled in the 1E rules for other supernaturals' blood for flavor.<br /> <br /> Wolves give you 2.5x the vitae, but for every 1 you drink you get -1 to frenzy checks because it's sort of wild and eggs your beast on. ( so it gives you endless vitae, but has a huge draw back )<br /> Changeling blood was 1-1 but it made you a bit.. loopy, like you were tripping on some acid.<br /> Demon blood was as human blood because you are drinking from the human cover not the actual demon ( though there might be something I missed in that )<br /> Sin-eater blood ( not sure if this is/was cannon or just a house rule ) but it tasted dead and made you see spirits.<br /> <br /> I know there is a thread somewhere about the effects of other supernaturals' blood.<br /> <br /> After some digging. Here it is: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...r-major-splats</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-12-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:26:54-07:00","id":864340,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem with calling a point of blood a pint's worth is that by the rules an average human could potentially survive having 6 points of blood taken. They'll be in bad shape, but by RAW as long as they have one unmarked health box they're not going to die. Losing 6/7ths of your blood in real life is rather more assuredly fatal.<br /> <br /> So it would make more sense to say that 7 health levels of vitae is the equivalent to what would kill a person, which is only about three and a half pints.<br /> <br /> Plus there's a merit now where a human can produce twice as much vitae as normal.<br /> <br /> Plus it's possible for someone with the Small Framed merit (and thus size 4) to have more health than someone with the Giant merit (and thus size 6) simply by having 3 more stamina. So someone who would certainly have less blood will produce more vitae.<br /> <br /> It's all very abstract, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:32:13-07:00","id":864345,"title":"","content":"I agree. Vitae should not be equated to pints of blood... as it's not actually blood. It's something that is created inside a vampire once blood is imbibed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:36:12-07:00","id":864347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member?p=864340#post864340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem with calling a point of blood a pint's worth is that by the rules an average human could potentially survive having 6 points of blood taken. They'll be in bad shape, but by RAW as long as they have one unmarked health box they're not going to die. Losing 6/7ths of your blood in real life is rather more assuredly fatal.<br /> <br /> So it would make more sense to say that 7 health levels of vitae is the equivalent to what would kill a person, which is only about three and a half pints.<br /> <br /> Plus there's a merit now where a human can produce twice as much vitae as normal.<br /> <br /> Plus it's possible for someone with the Small Framed merit (and thus size 4) to have more health than someone with the Giant merit (and thus size 6) simply by having 3 more stamina. So someone who would certainly have less blood will produce more vitae.<br /> <br /> It's all very abstract, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae isn't actual blood volume, it's taking the literal life-force of someone out of their pumping veins. The damage manifests in effects of fatigue, maybe some anemia, but not literal blood loss. In the case of drinking to the point a mortal would start to get aggravated damage, it's a case of his heart stopping, not of bleeding out.<br /> <br /> Otherwise elders would be like this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.comicmonsters.com/modules/Interviews/10YearsofBladeinterviews/Pearl.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:39:52-07:00","id":864351,"title":"","content":"Well, it's obviously not equivalent to blood volume <i>in a vampire</i>, but there could still be a distinct volume of regular blood that one must consume to process into a single point of vitae, even if this varies between individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:48:13-07:00","id":864355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member?p=864351#post864351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's obviously not equivalent to blood volume <i>in a vampire</i>, but there could still be a distinct volume of regular blood that one must consume to process into a single point of vitae, even if this varies between individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Is it worth figuring out mathmatically? Is it worth knowing for every 1 vitae you draw you took X Pint(s). The results after your character feeds is going to be the same... Your character will have inflicted 1 Lethal for every 1 vitae they created. and it will leave some people drained and others not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:50:20-07:00","id":864356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member?p=864355#post864355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it worth figuring out mathmatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. But that's not going to stop some nerd (*gestures at self*) figuring it out for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:11:10-07:00","id":864370,"title":"","content":"I believe there is another thread where someone tried. Might be a good baseline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:35:16-07:00","id":864495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/864291-endless-vitae-from-a-willing-uratha-pack-member?p=864370#post864370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there is another thread where someone tried. Might be a good baseline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The post you're talking about is in my thread here, I think, where we also discuss a lot of this blood volume stuff:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina\"> Estimating Stamina - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So! I kind of glossed over this at first, but feeding more than two points of Vitae on average is going to really mess people up. Effectively: Taking more Vitae than someone's Stamina gives them Drained. If one assumes an average of 2, that means 2 safe Vitae per vessel. Drained is brutal. -2 to all physical actions as well as rolls to stabilize and survive injury. Physical effort requires a Stamina roll or you pass out for an hour or more. They count being fed from (!), taking damage, or spending Willpower on a physical roll here. This means that your prey may well pass out once you take a point of </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}